{"type":"exercise","type_name":"Exercise","number":"","title":"A2","title_html":"A2","html":"<p>Verify from the table in <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"exm-dsn-adhesives\">@exm-dsn-adhesives</span> that the\ntreatment mean of adhesive 3 is <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"9.560\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c39\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c36\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9.560</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>, and compute the difference between\nadhesives 3 and 5 with its standard error. Is it significant by Tukey’s\ncriterion?</p>","file":"ch18-covariance-and-design/04-randomized-blocks.html"}